Look at the last two pages in
 http://www.biostat.jhsph.edu/~khansen/ggplot_density3.pdf
I find it completely counter-intuitive that the range of a different
group influences the plotting of the density of another group.  I find
it very counter-intuitive that the smoothness of the plotted density
depends on the range of the data.  I can see why this happens, but I
still think it is wrong and I also think it is strange when I plot to
a vector device.

